[{:db/id "q-47915/selection/1390b649ac8f5fa599cddb4e9919f8efddd426bbfa4d618c02d5e6bb854153a3" :answer/id #uuid "6854c36a-035a-52b7-8473-c146e56038ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=5$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" :answer/id #uuid "c34d4ce2-fd35-5755-ae97-2330aa24642e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915/selection/2bf1dd67714e170f87c922af4be9d1b901c810283ea5cea91fed0aeffa90bbd8" :answer/id #uuid "63f22c98-e5ea-5b29-b287-7fced162cf70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=5$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915/selection/beb070ff9437be85d24c175278ac7a31701d62c4c982ae60cf2212ad80210649" :answer/id #uuid "46e95f5f-eb72-5348-bd74-1fd5c7cb77d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[1,5]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "a045385b-5e56-5adc-83f4-e625d79c4785" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0f31a4d-e408-58d2-9646-d443d0447989" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47915/selection/beb070ff9437be85d24c175278ac7a31701d62c4c982ae60cf2212ad80210649" :answer-field/choices ["q-47915/selection/1390b649ac8f5fa599cddb4e9919f8efddd426bbfa4d618c02d5e6bb854153a3" "q-47915/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" "q-47915/selection/2bf1dd67714e170f87c922af4be9d1b901c810283ea5cea91fed0aeffa90bbd8" "q-47915/selection/beb070ff9437be85d24c175278ac7a31701d62c4c982ae60cf2212ad80210649" "q-47915/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47915" :question/id #uuid "6390010c-520d-5f4d-8e9b-7ad97c318ba0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47915" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/748abf694eac3c4e59fd09d3bc48648fe30e46561f536f9f9a16eac7eb526558.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown above. What are the $x$-coordinates of all the critical points?" :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that\n\n- at any point between  $x=1$ and $x=5$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ and\n\n- at $x=1$ and at $x=5$  there are sharp corners, hence ${f}^{′}(1)$ and ${f}^{′}(5)$ don't exist.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/48b786a6b9c270336ce507525acf2503439b2424dba59ed9ea200830a79dd828.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, all numbers in the closed interval $[1,5]$ are critical points for $f(x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47915/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection/262efaee666a88aace8a75783856ad0ced1ec64c45a854127f92d18b1f921056" :answer/id #uuid "df016bc0-b4ee-56d2-83d6-7e63864a8d91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "9121759a-0d14-5a06-bde3-3aba59bb816e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "53172910-3f6a-5916-bcfa-b58b71665829" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "ee65c5e2-2e0c-5a42-9345-ef5a410d0027" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "cf34da00-3c9c-5045-9857-9289dbf189d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8c9a23e-330d-59db-ab11-90c929b1ea8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47918/selection/262efaee666a88aace8a75783856ad0ced1ec64c45a854127f92d18b1f921056" :answer-field/choices ["q-47918/selection/262efaee666a88aace8a75783856ad0ced1ec64c45a854127f92d18b1f921056" "q-47918/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-47918/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-47918/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-47918/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47918" :question/id #uuid "126dc5db-7aa0-5e31-885e-35517971a655" :question/math-academy-id "q-47918" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/4a1843255ea718116bd2daa07f1375a3fb277c47ec8503fec90da824cd714d0b.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-2,10],$ which points represent the global maximum of $f(x)$ ?" :question/worked-solution "The global extrema of a function are the lowest or highest points of the function's graph over its entire domain.\n\nThe lowest point is the global minimum, whereas the highest point is the global maximum.\n\nAccording to the graph, the highest point is $D,$ and so this point represents the global maximum of $f(x).$ \n\n**Note:** The point $B$ is not a global maximum, it's a local maximum." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47918/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "7724e61e-8754-5ff2-b2d2-63d8accf12c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection/017ec74e48021b90d41305ba8cdc32b5df2a5e0d6620fb190ddde80f6dd00a99" :answer/id #uuid "218d63f5-bf0b-5234-a2f3-46f3cdf25280" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "d544b0cd-6e69-5c1e-a53d-e4ec5f98fab7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection/0b71ed31b54db2f2e7ec707b0a04499a5069d7189b0811622a9ab373f5143838" :answer/id #uuid "b416071b-693d-54a7-8b6f-60c43474ddf8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection/7a6d1d176b8642a56f2603d0a83dd054a16eb31e70d87fe78ade2a39774ad414" :answer/id #uuid "af50d4ef-c9cb-5b02-acf4-28e9686f045c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1201b52-31ab-51c5-82ce-d6f24e73cefb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73401/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer-field/choices ["q-73401/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-73401/selection/017ec74e48021b90d41305ba8cdc32b5df2a5e0d6620fb190ddde80f6dd00a99" "q-73401/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" "q-73401/selection/0b71ed31b54db2f2e7ec707b0a04499a5069d7189b0811622a9ab373f5143838" "q-73401/selection/7a6d1d176b8642a56f2603d0a83dd054a16eb31e70d87fe78ade2a39774ad414"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73401" :question/id #uuid "c043bdf3-7728-5760-8821-193ed1e72bf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73401" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/48569328379c72215884b759687c7c40ced06f9864d05d2638e4389694f90630.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points?" :question/worked-solution "A stationary point of $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at $x=0,$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/576d25a420f1f4ebcbd0e9b055d7a27159caa8f1721ff5f35a32b86c3e3a0fb3.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, there is only one stationary point, and its $x$-coordinate is $x=0.$\n\n**Note:** At $x=2$, there is a sharp corner, so ${f}^{′}(2)$ doesn't exist. This gives one more critical point. But this is not a stationary point." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73401/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6202b5e7-d6f4-55ac-9284-153f48291dbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "2d2800e2-2d27-5622-a6a1-f5992cc92489" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "70d1fc46-bc8c-5ff3-988a-209dc0f6ad30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6c0a2aff-d31f-5dc6-9481-56985c8e3b07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "fd0048b5-4130-5d93-bc47-76c1f1c47d63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7afee5-9159-52f5-88ce-0aa6c2474ac5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103437/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-103437/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-103437/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103437/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103437/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103437/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103437" :question/id #uuid "a63bb70d-731b-554c-adf7-37f9033998a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-103437" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/fb61c048eb7eac87f82c53717f8f67251b59610817ddf1f267e80543c0c86959.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=-1,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-1)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a critical point at $x=-1$ since each stationary point is a critical point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=-1$ since $f(-1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "1bbeab63-f015-57e1-85f1-08bd11c5c6a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "63273267-c257-5c62-8e89-2b50792f1d3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3cc3a8fc-b5aa-59b2-a411-b1f71fb7ac54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cd24d442-905c-56e7-b091-7fab665406c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "2042c9b3-c29e-5782-8171-8b3be12e32c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91463e95-1331-5fc1-a1c3-491eac483ed0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103438/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-103438/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-103438/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103438/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103438/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-103438/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103438" :question/id #uuid "d69f67de-ee43-5100-8b00-e925c0e6171b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103438" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011175/assets/5bbb0cacbe8dca2facfd49e757ba9b7aa40ee91ae820f001c72d637186d57b79.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement II is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1$ since $f(1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, all three statements are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103438/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
